## Summary

Implemented **`DET.CTA.LABEL_NONEMPTY`** as a deterministic DOM check: visible interactive controls must have a non-empty accessible name.

### Rule signal (from catalog)

Pass when every relevant **button/link** has a non-empty accessible name via `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `title`, visible text, `input` value, `img` alt, or screen-reader-only text.

### Files changed

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-cta-label-nonempty.check.js` | Full implementation: `collectCtaLabelNonemptyReport()` (Playwright `page.evaluate`), `findingsFromCtaLabelNonemptyReport()`, `run()` |
| `design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js` | Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **implemented** |
| `auditor-tests/det-cta-label-nonempty.test.js` | Unit tests for report mapping and `run()` |
| `design-rules/registry.generated.json` | Updated to `status: "implemented"` (coverage 16/34) |

### Implementation details

- Scans: `a[href]`, `button`, submit/reset/image inputs, `[role="button"]`, `[role="link"]`
- Skips hidden/invisible controls, `aria-hidden` subtrees, nested interactives, and disabled buttons
- **`MIN_CTA_LABEL_CHARS = 1`** (non-empty after trim)
- Findings: `severity: major`, `area: accessibility`, standard `message` / `evidence` / `remediation`
- Registry metadata: `accessibilitySemanticsMeta`, `priorityWeight: 8`

